<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore March manufacturing output falls 8.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore March manufacturing output falls 8.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's industrial production fell 8.5 percent year-on-year in March, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The EDB said in a statement the city-state's manufacturing output fell a revised 4.5 percent in February compared to the same month the year before.</p>
<p>Table of selected Singapore industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				    Mar 97	Feb 97	 Jan 97</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	-8.5	  -4.5	   -6.5</p>
<p>    Electronics		 -12.4	  -6.0	  -11.3</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	-16.6	  -9.6	   -1.5</p>
<p>    Pharmaceuticals	    -0.9	  29.4	    6.2</p>
<p>    Industrial chemicals     13.1	  11.5	    7.5</p>
<p>    Petrochemicals	     -9.7	   8.4	    8.9</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics   2.1	  -9.3	   -2.2</p>
<p>    Transport equipment	 3.3	  -9.3	   -5.9</p>
<p>    Fabricated metals	 -11.6	  -6.7	   -8.2</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	-0.5	  -3.0	    1.4</p>
<p>    Food &amp; Beverages	  -13.8	 -15.3	   -0.6</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	-2.0	 -11.1	   -6.6</p>
<p>    Plastic products	  -18.2	 -13.9	  -18.2</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
